 Vegas-area district that leans Democratic by about two points on the partisan baseline. He has raised $3.35 million and holds a large cash advantage over Republican Cody Whipple, a small-town rancher running an independent-minded campaign who has raised about $885,000. Two minor independent candidates also appear on the ballot.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals: expert ratings cluster at Likely Democratic, with several outlets rating the seat Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets give Horsford roughly 94 to 95 percent odds. Outside spending has been negligible, and coverage describes the district as flying under the radar. Whipple's distinctive profile and local issues such as Yucca Mountain have drawn attention, but the incumbency and financial advantages point clearly toward Horsford.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.37}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9577, "margin": 12.4}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9615, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9427, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9481, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9627, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9594, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9636, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9624, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 12.3}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9434, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9455, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.941, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9523, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9497, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9476, "margin": 12.4}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9443, "